--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,4 +13,18 @@ does not resolve: a missing member, an array index that is out of range, has a l
 (the nonexistent element after the last), or a scalar that is traversed. Only own members of objects
 are resolved, so `/__proto__` or `/toString` never reach inherited properties.
 
+## JSON Patch
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` (exported from `src/index.ts`) applies a JSON Patch
+([RFC 6902](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6902)) — an array of `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`,
+`copy` and `test` operations — and returns the resulting document. The input document and the patch are
+never mutated, and the result shares no structure with them. Operations apply in order; the first one
+that fails aborts the patch.
+
+It throws an `Error` when the patch is invalid (not an array, an operation that is not an object, an
+unknown `op`, a missing or invalid `path`, `from` or `value`) or when an operation fails: a missing
+target, an array index out of range, a failed `test`, a `move` into the value's own child, or a
+`remove` of the whole document (`path` `""`). Paths follow the JSON Pointer rules above. `test` compares
+values by JSON equality (member order is irrelevant).
+
 Run the tests with `npm test`.
